  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"any\" indicates that we use a universal quantifier, $\u2200.$\n\n- The words \"there exists\" indicate that we use an existential quantifier, $\u2203.$\n\n- The sentence refers to a real number and an integer. So, by denoting our numbers as $x$ and $n,$ respectively, we have\n\n$$\n\u2200\\,x\\in R,\\,\u2203\\,n\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as follows:\n\n$$\nx<n\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows:\n\n$\u2200\\,x\\in R,\\,\u2203\\,n\\in Z,\\,x<n$",
